Z||000000||kevin||05-14-2000||02:11 AM||||I may be over sentimental about keeping my interior as stock looking as possible, so adding speakers without gouging holes in the doors or asking my passenger to place some large awkward speakers on his lap while we drive is out of the question. I know you can update the 4x6 speakers in the sailpanels, and add new dash speakers, but has anyone added speakers in the center console area behind the 'dummy' grill; the grill that is right next to your shoulder as you drive? I think it is possible. Suggestions?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||05-14-2000||02:38 AM||||ok. think if you are going for a balanced system try this and still want to retain the stock look. I think you can replace the 4x10s with a 6" mid range woofer with slight mod might try a (5 1/4?) trimming the mounting plate/ slight mod to original hole. use a good 4x6 plate (I'm using Boston Acustics) and as for the small area in the console you might be able to get some small tweeters in there like the old Infinity ribbon tweeters. biggest problem is getting decent bass out of any area without alot of modification. I'm still looking into seeing if you can fit a 6" bazooka tube under the dash in the original sub location.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||05-14-2000||08:53 AM||||Actually that grill in the console is really there for a purpose, to ventilate and cool the ECM which is mounted back there. Before you plan some major modification, replace those wimpy factory speakers with some name brand, high quality, coaxial or 3-way speakers. I think you'll be very pleasantly surprised at how well they will sound in a small Fiero cockpit. If your ears need more at that point, then go for it. I think at that point, the only thing lacking is bass. I've mounted a 8" sub behind one seat and an amp behind the other. It works for me and it's all stock looking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-14-2000||09:35 AM||||Speaking of upgrading the stock speakers, I just happen to have a brand new set of 4x6s and 4x10s I'd just love to sell.  (Have I mentioned this before?!? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Uaana||05-14-2000||09:54 AM||||Just wondering how much do you want for your 4x10s?||||reg||5
Z||000005||Monkeyman||05-14-2000||09:59 AM||||I'd prefer to sell both sets together, but I suppose I'd start out @ $100.  If you're seriously interested, we might be able to talk a little.  They were $120 when I bought them a few months ago.  They've never even been out of the box.  (long story)  I've set my sights on a different speaker set up so I don't have to mess with cutting into the metal (for the rear speakers) on the Grape Ape ('85 GT).||||reg||1
